  "question": {
    "text": "Using the given figure, the ratio of \\(\\mathrm{R}_f\\) values of sample \\(\\mathrm{A}\\) and sample \\(\\mathrm{C}\\) is \\(x \\times 10^{-2}\\). Value of \\(x\\) is ______\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/bmL2ss07C0CNTpFf-bLV_lk0mG668apVCYHyuhMvAtc.original.fullsize.png\"><br>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "50",
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & \\mathrm{R}_{\\mathrm{f}} \\text { of } \\mathrm{A}=\\frac{5}{12.5} \\quad \\mathrm{R}_{\\mathrm{f}} \\text { of } \\mathrm{C}=\\frac{10}{12.5} \\\\ & \\text { Ratio }=\\frac{\\mathrm{R}_{\\mathrm{f}(\\mathrm{A})}}{\\mathrm{R}_{\\mathrm{f}(\\mathrm{C})}}=\\frac{1}{2}=0.5 \\text { or } 50 \\times 10^{-2}\\end{aligned}$",
